Package: mazegenerator
Title: Generate, Visualize, and Solve Random Mazes
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Matheus", email = "mat.fmc@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: An educational implementation of eleven classic maze generation
    algorithms -- randomized depth-first search, Prim, Kruskal, Wilson,
    Eller, recursive division, Aldous-Broder, hunt-and-kill, binary tree,
    sidewinder, and growing tree -- and nine pathfinding algorithms --
    A-star, Dijkstra, breadth-first search, greedy best-first search,
    bidirectional breadth-first search, bidirectional Dijkstra,
    bidirectional A* (NBA*), wall following, and dead-end filling, with a
    choice of A* heuristics (manhattan, euclidean, chebyshev, octile, or a
    custom function). Generate perfect or braided rectangular mazes, including
    shaped mazes carved through a mask, toroidal mazes that wrap at the
    edges, and mazes with open rooms; braid or sparsify a maze after the
    fact, and choose new start/end cells; compute comparative statistics
    on a maze's structure; visualize construction and solutions, export
    animated GIFs, and compare how the algorithms explore.
